Register the single-user speed knobs as vLLM env vars (vLLM 0.28.0).

VLLM_MARLIN_TUNE / VLLM_MARLIN_TUNE_DIR (tuned Marlin build, see marlin-tune/),
VLLM_SPEC_DECODE_ATTN (patches/spec-decode-attn.patch) and VLLM_DRAFT_TOPK_TOPP
(patches/sampler-small-topk-fast-softmax.patch). Every registered vLLM env var is
part of the torch.compile cache key; VLLM_MARLIN_TUNE in particular changes the
Marlin workspace tensor shape that is baked into the compiled graph, so without
this a cached graph from a run without the flag fails with
"assert_size_stride ... expected size 328==82". Independent of marlin-int8-layer-select.patch (same file, disjoint hunks):
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/speed-knobs-envs.patch

Env knobs this patch reads go through vllm.envs and are registered there (2026-09-15, the 0.28 hygiene pass; the
registry mirrors the raw defaults, and registration puts them in the torch.compile cache key): (none; read moved to the registry)

